From 177eb3b6bc277112a7c446a408732eeeec0a7e31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:34:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Use checked compact VM objects with native code pointers

Default LP64 builds to uint32_t handles while retaining legacy pointer-shaped OBJ for 32-bit C++ boards. Keep four-byte fields and GC forwarding words, protect allocator fill and byte-copy roots, and avoid signed tag/shift overflow. Make interpreter code and primitive pointers native-width and add a minimal C runtime profile.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
